Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-14T16:55:38.6907498Z   ISSUE_BODY: # Step 1: Protect your code
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	It's been a busy month at Mergington High! Your simple website for managing extra-curricular activities has really taken off. What started as a basic sign-up form for a few activities has grown into the go-to place for half the school activities. 📚✨
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	Principal Martinez was so impressed with your work that they announced at the last staff meeting that ALL clubs should start using the website. While this is exciting, you're a bit nervous - the last thing you want is an accidental change breaking the system right before the big Fall Activities Fair! 😰
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	When more teachers start helping with the Mergington High activities website, it's important to add some safeguards. Thankfully, GitHub provides several ways to protect your repository:
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. **Repository Rulesets** - These provide safeguards to limit:
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Pushing code directly to important branches
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Deleting or renaming branches
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Force pushing (which can overwrite history)
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - (and much more)
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. **`.gitignore`** - This special file tells Git which files it should NOT track, like:
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Temporary files that your code creates while running
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - Secret configuration files with sensitive information
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - System files that other developers don't need
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	> [!TIP]
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	> Think of these settings like the editorial process of a school yearbook. Various student committees will take photos and write articles, then the yearbook president will make adjustments to make sure everything flows together properly. Finally, a teacher/advisor will sign off that all content is appropriate.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	## ⌨️ Activity: (optional) Get to know our extracurricular activities site
