Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	## ⌨️ Activity: Add a branch ruleset
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	To get started, let's add some protections so that no one accidentally breaks the club registration system.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. If necessary, open another tab and navigate to this repository. We will start on the **Settings** tab.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the left navigation, expand the **Rules** area and select **Rulesets**.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Click the **New ruleset** dropdown and select **New branch ruleset**.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   <img width="250" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e9fd519-1421-4d6b-b654-a3fe53a8fb75" />
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Set the **Ruleset Name** as `Protect main` and change the **Enforcement status** to `Active`.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   <img width="250" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ce30fd34-39b5-4e22-b348-4af61fd05cd1" />
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Find the **Targets** section and use the **Add target** dropdown to add 2 entries:
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   1. Add the **Include default branch** option to ensure protections aren't bypassed by switching the default branch.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	      <img width="250" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/217263cc-d5c2-4ac0-b03c-a72494e5c812" />
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   1. Use the **include by pattern** option and enter the pattern `main`.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	      <img width="250" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/968c9ed8-b051-44eb-af42-d99670ad31fd" />
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	      <img width="250" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ddc52767-d93e-4c9e-a77a-90c3b5c08fb5" />
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Find the **Rules** section and ensure the following items are checked.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - [x] Restrict deletions
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - [x] Require a pull request before merging
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	     - Required approvals: `0`
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	     - [x] Require review from Code Owners
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   - [x] Block force pushes
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Scroll to the bottom and click the **Create** button to save the ruleset.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	## ⌨️ Activity: Create a `.gitignore` file
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	We know many teachers use different tools, so let's make sure they don't accidentally commit unnecessary files.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. At the top navigation, return to the **Code** tab and verify you are on the `main` branch.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Above the list of files, click the **Add file** dropdown and select **Create new file**.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   <img width="300" alt="New file button" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f3f8da8-1471-485a-9df5-8c03ecba2d8e"/>
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Enter the file name `.gitignore`. We will ignore the template selector for now and make our own. Copy the below example content into it.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   <img width="350" alt="preview of new file" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/580d1a63-a264-4d44-8901-50ad708b8822"/>
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```gitignore
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   # Python backend for club management
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   __pycache__/
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   *.py[cod]      # Python compiled files
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   *$py.class
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   *.so
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .Python
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   env/
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .env           # Where database passwords are stored
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   venv/          # Virtual environment for testing
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .venv
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   # Teacher IDE settings
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .vscode/       # Ms. Rodriguez uses VS Code
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .idea/         # Mr. Chen uses PyCharm
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   # Local development & testing
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   instance/
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .pytest_cache/
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .coverage      # Test coverage reports
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   htmlcov/
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   # Staff computer files
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   .DS_Store      # For teachers with Macs
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   Thumbs.db      # For teachers with Windows
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   ```
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. In the top right, select the **Commit changes...** button. Notice that it won't let us commit to the `main` branch! Our ruleset is working! Nice!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	   <img width="400" alt="image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e85948d-75c8-4c13-8ddd-4707bf9b0805" />
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Enter `prepare-to-collaborate` for the branch name then click the **Propose changes** button. You will be forwarded to a new page to start a new pull request.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. Set the title to `Prepare to collaborate` and click the **Create pull request** button. **Do NOT merge yet**, since we will be adding more collaboration related changes.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	1. With the file committed, wait a moment for Mona to check your work, provide feedback, and share the next lesson.
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	> [!TIP]
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	> GitHub and the community have built a repository with [sample `.gitignore` files](https://github.com/github/gitignore) for many situations. Make sure to check it out!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	<details>
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	<summary>🤷 Having trouble?</summary><br/>
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	Make sure you pushed the `.gitignore` file to `prepare-to-collaborate` branch. Exact naming for both matters!
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	
Post next step content	UNKNOWN STEP	</details>
